### Trade Settlement Simulator - HTTP Requests
# Compatible with VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ IDEA, and httpyac CLI

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Verify Initial Account Balances
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Accept: application/json

### 2. Capture a New Trade (PENDING)
# @name createHappyTrade
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-trade-001

{
  "side": "BUY",
  "isin": "US0378331005",
  "quantity": 100.00,
  "price": 150.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "ourPartyId": "HOUSE-01",
  "counterpartyId": "COUNTERPARTY-01",
  "tradeDate": "2026-10-29",
  "settlementDate": "2026-10-30"
}

### 3. Read Back Newly Created Trade
GET {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createHappyTrade.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Counterparty Confirmation with Mismatch -> UNMATCHED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createHappyTrade.id}}/confirmation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-confirm-mismatch-001

{
  "side": "SELL",
  "isin": "US0378331005",
  "quantity": 100.00,
  "price": 160.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 5. Correct Counterparty Confirmation -> MATCHED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createHappyTrade.id}}/confirmation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-confirm-match-001

{
  "side": "SELL",
  "isin": "US0378331005",
  "quantity": 100.00,
  "price": 150.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 6. Custodian Settlement Result -> SETTLED (Atomic DVP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createHappyTrade.id}}/settlement-instruction-result
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-settle-001

{
  "result": "SETTLED",
  "reason": "settle_success"
}

### 7. Inspect Settled Trade Audit Trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createHappyTrade.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Inspect Updated Account Balances
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Accept: application/json

### 9. Failure Flow - Capture Trade Exceeding Counterparty Cash
# COUNTERPARTY-01 buys 1,000 shares @ €100.00 = €100,000 required, but only holds €40,000 cash
# @name createFailTrade
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-trade-fail-001

{
  "side": "SELL",
  "isin": "US0378331005",
  "quantity": 1000.00,
  "price": 100.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "ourPartyId": "HOUSE-01",
  "counterpartyId": "COUNTERPARTY-01",
  "tradeDate": "2026-10-29",
  "settlementDate": "2026-10-30"
}

### 10. Confirm Trade 2 -> MATCHED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}/confirmation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-confirm-fail-001

{
  "side": "BUY",
  "isin": "US0378331005",
  "quantity": 1000.00,
  "price": 100.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 11. Attempt Settlement with Insufficient Funds -> FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}/settlement-instruction-result
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-settle-fail-001

{
  "result": "SETTLED",
  "reason": "settle_success"
}

### 12. Retry Failed Trade -> MATCHED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}/retry
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-retry-001

### 13. Simulate Custodian Notice of Rejection -> FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}/settlement-instruction-result
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-custodian-reject-001

{
  "result": "FAILED",
  "reason": "custodian_rejected"
}

### 14. Cancel Failed Trade -> CANCELLED
POST {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}/cancel
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-suite-cancel-001

### 15. Verify Cancelled Trade Read Model
GET {{baseUrl}}/trades/{{createFailTrade.id}}
Accept: application/json
